    feat: the staged workspace holds the project
    
    TESP 5.3 step 4 says stage the project files, and the code created the directory
    and put a .keep in it. The slot has been in the layout since v1.1 and has never
    been filled, which is why a builder dispatched into it concludes the project is
    empty -- which is what happened to SCHOTTY's round.
    
    The kernel and the owner's configuration are never staged. A staged workspace is
    what a builder can reach, and 7.3 grants it no access to installed kernel files,
    so copying those in would move them from unreachable to readable -- the one thing
    staging must not do. The probe caught that leak; it would have shipped silently.
    
    Also corrects the v1.12 status line: it claimed owner acceptance, which is wrong
    twice over. The owner's remit is the VISP and the FUSP, and 20 says this layer is
    not separately gated. It rests on the workshop's LLM authority, and now says so.

